ons (who said what)","f":"Etymology","b":"Old French cerchier, to seek or search; research = re-searching","k":"b"},{"i":"n9f6bbdb44c","c":"4","t":"Definitions (who said what)","f":"Thomas and Nelson (1996)","b":"careful and systematic means of solving problems","k":"b"},{"i":"ncaeaccaf30","c":"4","t":"Definitions (who said what)","f":"Merton","b":"develops theory: clarifies, initiates, reformulates, refocuses","k":"b"},{"i":"nf18727a92b","c":"4","t":"Definitions (who said what)","f":"Wiersma (1995)","b":"process; recognized methods of data collection, analysis, interpretation","k":"b"},{"i":"n29297f4f3f","c":"4","t":"Definitions (who said what)","f":"Good","b":"systematic, defensible pursuit; ordered, reasonable, communicable","k":"b"},{"i":"n29ebd6ffb2","c":"4","t":"Definitions (who said what)","f":"Aquino","b":"systematic search for pertinent information, then the research report","k":"b"},{"i":"n6866a67704","c":"4","t":"Definitions (who said what)","f":"Mnemonic","b":"Thomas Solves, Merton builds Theory, Wiersma has Methods, Good is O-R-C, Aquino writes the Report","k":"b"},{"i":"n22c9a8974d","c":"4","t":"Essential factors (3 Ms)","f":"Money","b":"printing, advisers, panelists, validators, analysts, tokens","k":"b"},{"i":"ncccfcbbb9e","c":"4","t":"Essential factors (3 Ms)","f":"Materials","b":"paper, computer, printer, instruments","k":"b"},{"i":"n5bf04925ae","c":"4","t":"Essential factors (3 Ms)","f":"Men","b":"researchers, advisers, panelists, experts","k":"b"},{"i":"n1189a69108","c":"4","t":"Good research by author","f":"De Leon and Claudio (4)","b":"produces processible, specific, generalizable, interpretable results","k":"b"},{"i":"n5f558b230e","c":"4","t":"Good research by author","f":"Best (7)","b":"gathers new data, solves problems, develops sound theories, requires expertise, accurate observation and description, logical and objective, carefully recorded and reported","k":"b"},{"i":"n68ad606401","c":"4","t":"Good research by author","f":"Thomas and Nelson (5)","b":"systematic, logical, empirical, reductive, replicable (S-L-E-R-R)","k":"b"},{"i":"ne0a4ed9e91","c":"4","t":"Good research by author","f":"Leedy (7)","b":"begins with a question, requires a plan, clear statement of the problem, subproblems, hypotheses, facts and their meaning, circular","k":"b"},{"i":"nb624c74e9e","c":"4","t":"Tricky meanings","f":"Replicable","b":"same variables with another method (or vice versa); not duplicable","k":"b"},{"i":"nd6c3beb821","c":"4","t":"Tricky meanings","f":"Reductive","b":"reduced to its simplest interpretation","k":"b"},{"i":"nd639665737","c":"4","t":"Tricky meanings","f":"Empirical","b":"gives evidence and support","k":"b"},{"i":"n52012926bc","c":"4","t":"Tricky meanings","f":"Circular","b":"the recommendation becomes a new problem","k":"b"},{"i":"na71da409c0","c":"4","t":"Tricky meanings","f":"Specific","b":"each sub-question has its own result/table","k":"b"},{"i":"nf4e90fe8e5","c":"4","t":"Tricky meanings","f":"Communicable (Good)","b":"can be interpreted","k":"b"},{"i":"n61809ad717","c":"4","t":"Difficulties","f":"Recognizing problems","b":"read literature, past recommendations and limitations; observe","k":"b"},{"i":"nc67f089a7c","c":"4","t":"Difficulties","f":"Duplication","b":"copying a whole study (replication is fine)","k":"b"},{"i":"n8e208d9d45","c":"4","t":"Difficulties","f":"Indifference of people","b":"use inclusion and exclusion criteria","k":"b"},{"i":"nd1ce145848","c":"4","t":"Good researcher (Calmorin, 2004)","f":"R","b":"research-oriented","k":"b"},{"i":"nc2c6ce8844","c":"4","t":"Good researcher (Calmorin, 2004)","f":"E","b":"efficient (revise right away)","k":"b"},{"i":"n3117fad60c","c":"4","t":"Good researcher (Calmorin, 2004)","f":"S","b":"scientific (cross-check AI; no Wikipedia)","k":"b"},{"i":"nc2c6ce8844x","c":"4","t":"Good researcher (Calmorin, 2004)","f":"E","b":"effective (does what the panel asks)","k":"b"},{"i":"nd3f6cc54c5","c":"4","t":"Good researcher (Calmorin, 2004)","f":"A","b":"active (finds replacement participants)","k":"b"},{"i":"nd1ce145848x","c":"4","t":"Good researcher (Calmorin, 2004)","f":"R","b":"resourceful (finds another way)","k":"b"},{"i":"nf2b0c40961","c":"4","t":"Good researcher (Calmorin, 2004)","f":"C","b":"creative (varied sentences, no run-ons)","k":"b"},{"i":"nafbbf30e67","c":"4","t":"Good researcher (Calmorin, 2004)","f":"H","b":"honest","k":"b"},{"i":"nc2c6ce8844xx","c":"4","t":"Good researcher (Calmorin, 2004)","f":"E","b":"economical (online interviews, useful tokens)","k":"b"},{"i":"nd1ce145848xx","c":"4","t":"Good researcher (Calmorin, 2004)","f":"R","b":"religious (honest, unaltered results)","k":"b"},{"i":"nd83372c03d","c":"4","t":"Proposal tips (lecture)","f":"Requirement","b":"no finals exam: defend the proposal individually (prefinal), then the final paper","k":"b"},{"i":"n7f906577bb","c":"4","t":"Proposal tips (lecture)","f":"System","b":"problem → theory → objectives → SOP → instrument → methods → results → summary → conclusion → recommendation","k":"b"},{"i":"n42113fed7a","c":"4","t":"Proposal tips (lecture)","f":"Parallelism","b":"3 SOP questions = 3 tables = 3 discussions = 3 summaries = 3 conclusions","k":"b"},{"i":"n38d2e8a311","c":"4","t":"Proposal tips (lecture)","f":"Titles","b":"spell out acronyms; no design; no \"negative\" (biased); specific and time-bounded (SMART)","k":"b"},{"i":"n7f0b26f774","c":"4","t":"Proposal tips (lecture)","f":"Theory","b":"framework for quanti (required, gives the indicators); lens for quali (may be left out)","k":"b"},{"i":"nc341f5d8fc","c":"4","t":"Proposal tips (lecture)","f":"Hypotheses","b":"difference (comparative), relationship (correlational), influence (causal), effect (experimental); none for single-variable descriptive or qualitative","k":"b"},{"i":"n69ba8afe49","c":"4","t":"Proposal tips (lecture)","f":"Likert","b":"mean, description, interpretation (interpretation goes in the conclusion)","k":"b"},{"i":"n60ac07c4d6","c":"4","t":"Proposal tips (lecture)","f":"Qualitative","b":"implications, not conclusions; member checking; debriefer","k":"b"},{"i":"n315b9b3993","c":"4","t":"Proposal tips (lecture)","f":"Ethics","b":"validators get 3+ days and decent snacks; collect only needed data (RA 10173)","k":"b"}]}